ch easier on a  computer than in real life anyone can be  a superhero when you've got cg to help  you out who needs to spend all that time  and effort destroying real cars when you  can let electrifying cg powers do all  the heavy lifting in visual effects  sometimes you gotta do it sometimes  there's no other way literally the bit  of glow and lens flare we get when  seeing these powers on screen were added  purposefully to help bring a more  grounded feel to the show number four  how long could he hang on chase crawford  had the special privilege of being able  to film riding the whale on somewhat of  an actual whale he's a pretty cool dude  and he was just like all right cool man  whatever i think it was also just kind  of hilarious for him in what was the  only blue screenshot filmed in the  entire sequence is crawford sitting atop  a kind of mechanical bull whale 12 feet  up in the air chase just kind of trusted  us the actor had a solid grip feeling  that power as he filmed what would  become a very eye-catching shot guys yo  you know like big bear hug  and dolphins number five you gotta break  it down one step at a time launching  someone into a building is shockingly  easy to film that is if you consider an  actor making the leap out of a building  so the footage can be played in reverse  easy as for making the building explode  well it was a bit more complicated than  that the vfx version of the building  itself was the star of the show every  bit of the structure was detailed which  ensured the explosion and blast would  look as realistic as possible every beam  every stair and every cg brick was laid  before destroying it all anyway but for  a shot like this all that work is worth  it  number six three  two  one it's an efficient way to travel  you've got to give them that the fact  that it looks electrifyingly cool is  just a bonus wires were in place to  raise those performers up but the cool  effects well that was all the cg team  number seven need a s